{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"MGASA-2026-0314","published":"2026-08-03T18:47:23Z","modified":"2026-08-03T19:00:05.541827422Z","upstream":["CVE-2023-35789","CVE-2026-44235","CVE-2026-44236"],"summary":"Updated librabbitmq packages fix security vulnerabilities","details":"The updated packages fix security vulnerabilities:\nAn issue was discovered in the C AMQP client library (aka rabbitmq-c)\nthrough 0.13.0 for RabbitMQ. Credentials can only be entered on the\ncommand line (e.g., for amqp-publish or amqp-consume) and are thus\nvisible to local attackers by listing a process and its arguments.\n(CVE-2023-35789)\nsize_t underflow in AMQP frame length computation leads to out-of-bounds\nread in rabbitmq-c. (CVE-2026-44235)\nHeap buffer overflow in AMQP login handshake via undersized\nconnection.tune.frame_max. (CVE-2026-44236)\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"librabbitmq","ecosystem":"Mageia:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/mageia/librabbitmq?arch=source&distro=mageia-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.15.0-2.1.mga10"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"section":"core"},"database_specific":{"source":"https://advisories.mageia.org/MGASA-2026-0314.json"}},{"package":{"name":"librabbitmq","ecosystem":"Mageia:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/mageia/librabbitmq?arch=source&distro=mageia-9"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.11.0-1.1.mga9"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"section":"core"},"database_specific":{"source":"https://advisories.mageia.org/MGASA-2026-0314.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://advisories.mageia.org/MGASA-2026-0314.html"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugs.mageia.org/show_bug.cgi?id=35702"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00254.html"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/alanxz/rabbitmq-c/security/advisories/GHSA-9mmv-r8g3-qp46"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/alanxz/rabbitmq-c/security/advisories/GHSA-jh48-qjf5-fx5v"},{"type